  "final_message": "Done. The leaderboard app is complete and verified with 90 end-to-end API checks.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite under `./data/app.db` (users, tokens, scores), bcrypt-style hashing via werkzeug, bearer tokens (hashed at rest, survive restarts).\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201, `admin` name reserved), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\"}`; admin only when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set at startup, read per-request so sign-in stays disabled when unset)\n- `GET /api/leaderboard` \u2014 one row per player, best *visible* score per period (today = UTC midnight, week = Monday 00:00 UTC, all), competition ranking, `period`/`limit`/`player` (case-insensitive substring, ranks stay global)\n- `POST /api/scores` (201, server-stamped `achieved_at`, returns `rank` + `personal_best`), `GET /api/scores` (newest first incl. own hidden rows, `best_score` excludes hidden)\n- `GET /api/admin/scores` (paginated), `POST /api/admin/scores/{id}/toggle`; unauthenticated \u2192 401 on protected routes; SPA fallback + JSON 404s under `/api`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4): sign-in/register panel, header with username + sign-out, leaderboard (rank/medal badges for top 3, highlighted own row, Today/This week/All-time tabs, player search, refresh), score form showing rank and \"New personal best!\", submissions list with best score, admin table with hide/show + pagination. No hand-written CSS beyond `src/index.css` (Tailwind entry).\n\n**Scaffold fix**: `backend/requirements.txt` now carries hashes for the resolved set \u2014 pip's `--require-hashes` (triggered by the hashed `requirements.lock` constraints) rejected the bare pins and would have failed the Docker build; both install modes now work unchanged with the existing Dockerfile.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
